README
# Repo Dashboard

## Setup

1. `npm install`
2. `cp config.example.js config.js` and fill in your own repos/links/SSH details.
3. `npm start`

Everything user-specific lives in `config.js` — repo list, work links, SSH
host/user/password for the PMC scan, and SSH user/password for connecting to
a device. Nothing is hardcoded in the app itself anymore, so anyone can reuse
it by just editing that one file. `config.js` is gitignored; `config.example.js`
is the template that's safe to commit.

## Why the app was closing itself

`package.json` was building the Windows target as `"portable"`. A portable
NSIS build extracts the app into a temp folder at launch and **that temp
folder gets cleaned up automatically after a while, even if the app is still
running.** Once `config.js` and other app files disappear out from under the
running process, it crashes — which is exactly the "runs fine, then exits
later" symptom.

This build now targets a plain `zip` output instead (see `build.win.target`
in `package.json`). Unzip it once to a normal folder and run the exe from
there — it won't self-destruct. If you'd rather ship a real installer,
switch the target to `"nsis"` (non-portable) instead of `"portable"`.

Other things fixed along the way:

- **Config path**: `config.js` used to be resolved via `process.cwd()`,
  which isn't reliable once the app is packaged. It's now resolved relative
  to the exe (packaged) or the project root (dev), and a missing/broken
  config shows a proper dialog instead of crashing.
- **WSL detection**: checked once at startup and cached (`shellRunner.js`),
  instead of re-running `wsl --status` on every single click. If WSL isn't
  available, everything automatically falls back to PowerShell.
- **SSH commands now have a timeout** (`ConnectTimeout` + exec timeout), so
  an unreachable host can't hang forever and pile up stuck processes.
- **Single instance lock** so you can't accidentally end up with multiple
  copies fighting over the same terminal windows.
- Split the one giant HTML file into proper files: `index.html`,
  `styles.css`, `renderer.js`, `main.js`, `preload.js`, `shellRunner.js`.
  The old file had the renderer script duplicated in two places — that's
  consolidated into a single `renderer.js` now.

## Files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `main.js` | Electron main process: window, config loading, all shell commands |
| `preload.js` | Safe bridge exposing `window.electronAPI` to the renderer |
| `shellRunner.js` | WSL detection (cached) + exec wrapper with timeouts |
| `index.html` / `styles.css` / `renderer.js` | The UI |
| `config.example.js` | Template — copy to `config.js` |
| `config.js` | Your actual config (gitignored) |

## Building

```
npm run build
```

Produces a zip under `dist/`. Unzip it somewhere permanent and run the exe
from there.

